# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Hermes WebUI — Legacy Env (DEPRECATED)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This file is kept for backward compatibility.
# The canonical, generic environment template now lives in:
#   hermes-webui-docker/.env.example
#
# That file supports all the same variables (and more), with full inline
# documentation and sensible defaults. New projects should copy from there.
#
#   cd hermes-webui-docker
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file simply re-exports the same values for compatibility.
#

UID=1000
GID=1000

HERMES_HOME_HOST_PATH=${DEVCONTAINER_HOST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT}/.hermes-web-ui-home
HERMES_WORKSPACE_HOST_PATH=${DEVCONTAINER_HOST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT}
